esp32s31 SMP parity: per-hart idle policy; hosted-HID attach before the HID bus

Files (whole): arch/riscv/kernel/process.c, drivers/hid/esp32s31-hosted-hid.c
(and patches/0051's CLIC driver refreshed: global poll removed, false
"hart0 frozen" panic removed).

process.c arch_cpu_idle(): with a second CPU online hart 1 does not wfi (a
cross-hart pending bit does not wake it) and just returns; the lent CPU DOES
wfi - it traps to the hart0 monitor, which leaves the exception and blocks in
FreeRTOS until something is pending. Replaces cpu_idle_poll_ctrl(true), which
made the lent CPU spin through the trap 460,000 times/s on the shared bus
(gate canaries +11%) and starved hart0's IDLE task.

esp32s31-hosted-hid.c: hid_add_device() -EINVAL (HID bus not registered yet)
now re-queues the attach every 100 ms, up to 10 s. hart0 announces its USB
devices ~4.8 s after reset regardless; on an SMP boot that beat hid_init()
and the keyboard and mouse were lost for the whole boot (gate: attach=0).
